Restore the web client's last active workspace after a restart

After a workspace restart the tile lands on Landing - "Select a workspace from
the sidebar to begin" - even though the sidebar lists every worktree.

Upstream's paired-client session read already restores this from
`ui.lastActiveRepoId` and `ui.lastActiveWorktreeId`, but nothing anywhere writes
those two fields: the producer was never implemented, on desktop or on web.
`rememberWebActiveWorkspace` records the pointer from the web session adapter
through the existing `ui.set` RPC, which persists into the host's own `ui`
slice, so a browser with empty storage still restores;
`getStoredWorkspaceSession` falls back to the browser's sanitized copy when the
host pointer is absent. The pointer is built from the keys the caller actually
sent - `session.patch` passes a raw `Partial`, and coercing an absent key to
null would clear the other half, since the restore's fallback cannot fall
through a stored null - so the unchanged half is carried forward. The browser
copy is written before the active-environment check: an unpaired client should
still reopen where it left off.

To test, open a worktree in the tile, restart the workspace, and reload: that
worktree should be active. Switch worktrees within a repo and reload again - the
repo must not be lost. Repeat in a browser with cleared storage. Covered by
`web-preload-api.test.ts` and
`web-preload-api-active-workspace-pointer.test.ts`.
